# Ubuntu's traditional sources.list has been replaced by DEB822-format
# sources managed by /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ubuntu.sources.
#
# This file exists deliberately empty (matching what real official
# Ubuntu 26.04 images ship) rather than being absent entirely -
# subiquity's own apt configurer (subiquity/server/apt.py) renames this
# exact path away during install and back again once it's done. The
# "away" half is wrapped in contextlib.suppress(FileNotFoundError), so
# it tolerates this file's absence just fine, but the final "back" half
# is not similarly guarded - confirmed the hard way via a live crash at
# the very last step of an otherwise fully successful install:
# FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory:
# '/target/etc/apt/sources.list'. Shipping this placeholder gives that
# rename-away/rename-back roundtrip something to actually round-trip.
#
# See /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ubuntu.sources for the actual configuration.
